 "statement": {
  "status": "present",
  "value": "records[0] is a header of distinct field names that includes \"id\"; every later row holds one string per field and the ids are distinct and non-empty. weights holds \"<field>:<weight>\" strings naming distinct non-id header fields, each weight a decimal in [0, 1] with at most 4 decimal places, summing to exactly 1; unlisted fields weigh 0. threshold is a number in [0, 1] with at most 4 decimal places. The similarity of two records is the sum of the weights of the weighted fields on which both hold the same non-empty value (an empty value never matches); two records are linked when their similarity is at least threshold. All weight arithmetic is exact (decimal, not binary floating point). Level 3: return one string per data row: the id of the other record with the highest similarity among those linked to it, the earliest row on a tie, or \"\" when no record is linked to it.",
  "provenance": [
